<title>UK: ICCO details result of cocoa buffer stock sale.</title>
<headline>ICCO details result of cocoa buffer stock sale.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The International Cocoa Organization (ICCO) said the 4,250 tonne buffer-stock sale earlier on Wednesday was completed at the following prices.</p>
<p> ORIGIN	    TONNES	QUALITY	U.S. DOLLAR</p>
<p>PRICE/TONNE</p>
<p> Ivory Coast	  126	   GF	     $1,575</p>
<p> Ivory Coast	   50	   GF	     $1,575</p>
<p> Ivory Coast	   50	   FF	     $1,512</p>
<p> Ivory Coast	  928	   GF	     $1,533 - 1,561</p>
<p> Ivory Coast	1,221	   FF	     $1,479 - 1,512</p>
<p> Ghana		  147	   GF	     $1,594</p>
<p> Ghana		   97	   FF	     $1,525</p>
<p> Nigeria		197	   GF	     $1,564</p>
<p> Nigeria		101	   FF	     $1,485</p>
<p> Nigeria		  5	   GF	     $1,564</p>
<p> Nigeria		158	   FF	     $1,485</p>
<p> Togo		    99	   GF	     $1,574</p>
<p> Ivory Coast	  100	  FAQ	     $1,270</p>
<p> Ivory Coast	   98	  FAQ	     $1,270</p>
<p> Ivory Coast	  101	  FAQ	     $1,388</p>
<p> Ivory Coast	  422	  FAQ	     $1,270 - 1,388</p>
<p> Nigeria		 40	  FAQ	     $1,346</p>
<p> Nigeria		 63	  FAQ	     $1,298</p>
<p> Nigeria		248	  FAQ	     $1,270 - 1,430</p>
<p>(GF=good fermented, FF=fair fermented, FAQ=fair to average quality)</p>
<p>The ICCO said the carry for forward delivery was calculated at $12 per tonne per month.</p>
<p>--Christopher Lyddon,  London Newsroom 044 71 542 7928.</p>
